    "q-213406": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213406",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following integers has a multiplicative inverse modulo $42?$\n\nI. $12$\n\nII. $25$\n\nIII. $37$",
      "worked_solution": "An integer $a$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $n$ if and only if $a$ and $n$ are coprime, i.e., $\\text{gcd}(a,n)=1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- $12$ does *not* have a multiplicative inverse modulo $42$ since $\\text{gcd}(12,42)=6\\ne 1.\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- $25$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $42$ since $\\text{gcd}(25,42)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $37$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $42$ since $\\text{gcd}(37,42)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
